13
00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:16.821
A mattress.

14
00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:20.325
And a blanket!

15
00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.243
A microfiber one.

16
00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:24.579
And a portable toilet too.

17
00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:28.124
No more to spend!

18
00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.724
So food and drinks are provided.

19
00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.435
What about a table?

20
00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:49.854
Protein.

21
00:03:52.815 --> 00:03:53.900
Iron.

22
00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:55.360
Perfect.

23
00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.421
How pretty!

24
00:05:24.782 --> 00:05:26.868
Your expressions are so funny!

25
00:05:28.619 --> 00:05:29.495
"Funny"?

26
00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:34.625
We just learned that the prize money
for each room is different.

27
00:05:34.709 --> 00:05:37.086
Everyone should share theirs.

28
00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:38.713
How much do you all get?

29
00:05:38.796 --> 00:05:39.714
For me.

30
00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.633
{\an8}80.000 won a minute.

31
00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:43.801
{\an8}You get 80.000?

32
00:05:44.427 --> 00:05:45.678
{\an8}I get 30.000 won.

33
00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.098
{\an8}-20.000 won.
-130.000 for me.

34
00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.142
{\an8}Wait. What is this?

35
00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:52.935
{\an8}Everyone's is different?

36
00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:55.313
And you. 7th Floor?

37
00:05:55.396 --> 00:05:57.273
How much do you make a minute?

38
00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.816
{\an8}I get 210.000 won.

39
00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.695
{\an8}And 8th Floor
should get exactly 340.000 won.

40
00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:05.573
{\an8}How do you know?

41
00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:09.202
{\an8}Did you just calculate the numbers
in your head?

42
00:06:09.285 --> 00:06:13.998
No. If you think about the prize money
going from the 1st to the 8th floor.

43
00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:15.625
there's a pattern.

44
00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.754
If you add the two preceding numbers.
you get the next one.

45
00:06:20.254 --> 00:06:22.382
1st Floor said he gets 10.000 won.

46
00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.092
2nd Floor gets 20.000.

47
00:06:24.175 --> 00:06:25.218
Yes.

48
00:06:25.301 --> 00:06:26.552
You're right.

49
00:06:26.636 --> 00:06:29.138
Yes. Add those two numbers.
and you get three.

50
00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.808
That's why 3rd Floor
is getting 30.000 won.

51
00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.768
Yes. it's 30.000 won for me.

52
00:06:33.851 --> 00:06:36.813
I'm right above 3rd Floor
on the 4th floor.

53
00:06:37.438 --> 00:06:40.566
so if I add 2nd Floor's 20.000
and 3rd Floor's 30.000. yes.

54
00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.567
I get 50.000 won.

55
00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:44.737
Wait. I'm getting 80.000 won. so…

56
00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:47.490
That's the sum of 3rd Floor
and 4th Floor's prize money.

57
00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.658
Then the next floor--

58
00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.827
6th Floor's is five plus eight.
which is 130.000 won.

59
00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.955
The same goes for me.
and I get 210.000 won.

60
00:06:54.038 --> 00:06:55.415
That's how 8th Floor gets…

61
00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:58.376
340.000 won.

62
00:06:59.627 --> 00:07:00.711
Yes. that's right.

63
00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:03.548
It's the Fibonacci sequence.

64
00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.261
I've heard of that.

65
00:07:08.344 --> 00:07:11.431
But what does it have to do
with our prize money?

66
00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:12.765
Why does it apply here?

67
00:07:12.849 --> 00:07:15.435
I wouldn't know the hosts' intentions.

68
00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.312
but they seem like an interesting lot.

69
00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:20.982
The Fibonacci sequence

70
00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.484
creates a golden ratio.

71
00:07:23.568 --> 00:07:25.403
-A golden ratio?
-Yes.

72
00:07:25.903 --> 00:07:27.321
In a Fibonacci sequence.

73
00:07:27.405 --> 00:07:30.116
if you divide a number
by its preceding number.

74
00:07:30.199 --> 00:07:35.621
the ratio converges to approximately 1.6
as the numbers increase.

75
00:07:35.705 --> 00:07:37.874
This 1 to 1.6 ratio
is called the golden ratio

76
00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:41.752
because. for humans.
it provides a sense of security

77
00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:43.963
and is perceived as beautiful.

78
00:07:44.046 --> 00:07:46.424
For example. the ratio
of a credit card's dimensions

79
00:07:46.507 --> 00:07:47.967
is close to the golden ratio.

80
00:07:48.676 --> 00:07:53.431
Coincidentally. the floor cards
we picked up on our way in…

81
00:07:54.015 --> 00:07:55.808
Are the size of a credit card.

82
00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:57.810
But isn't this unfair?

83
00:07:58.853 --> 00:08:00.480
This was all random.

84
00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:01.856
This is really fucked up.

85
00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:03.691
You're the ones who picked them.

86
00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:08.154
Stop whining.
and let's take a look at everyone's rooms.

87
00:08:10.364 --> 00:08:14.327
<i>8th Floor gets 340.000 per minute.</i>
<i>489.6 million won a day.</i>

88
00:08:16.078 --> 00:08:19.957
<i>7th Floor gets 210.000 per minute.</i>
<i>302.4 million won a day.</i>

89
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:24.545
<i>6th Floor gets 130.000 per minute.</i>
<i>187.2 million won a day.</i>

90
00:08:26.088 --> 00:08:29.550
<i>5th Floor gets 80.000 per minute.</i>
<i>115.2 million won a day.</i>

91
00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.804
<i>4th Floor gets 50.000 per minute.</i>
<i>72 million won a day.</i>

92
00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:37.850
<i>3rd Floor gets 30.000 per minute.</i>
<i>43.2 million won a day.</i>

93
00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:42.939
<i>2nd Floor gets 20.000 per minute.</i>
<i>28.8 million won a day.</i>

94
00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.276
This is so damn small.

95
00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.819
Watch your head.

96
00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:52.448
<i>1st Floor gets 10.000 per minute.</i>
<i>14.4 million won a day.</i>

97
00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:55.159
This is so annoying.

98
00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:59.372
I could've chosen the 8th floor.

99
00:09:00.665 --> 00:09:02.792
No point regretting it now.

100
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.086
We chose the cards at random.

101
00:09:06.128 --> 00:09:09.715
I didn't get much choice.
There were only two cards left.

102
00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:11.968
You still managed to pick
better than I did.

103
00:09:12.843 --> 00:09:14.178
And. you know…

104
00:09:16.806 --> 00:09:21.018
What kind of show doesn't provide
such important information?

105
00:09:21.811 --> 00:09:24.438
This should be illegal.
We should report it.

106
00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:26.524
Still. you guys are so lucky.

107
00:09:27.984 --> 00:09:31.487
I thought 10.000 won per minute was a lot.

108
00:09:31.988 --> 00:09:34.240
Oh. 1st Floor.

109
00:09:35.157 --> 00:09:36.033
I'm sorry.

110
00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:38.077
We should've been more considerate.

111
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:38.995
Sorry?

112
00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:41.330
Please don't be!

113
00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.419
I wasn't trying to make you uncomfortable.
I was just unlucky.

114
00:09:46.502 --> 00:09:48.337
I had other cards to pick from.

115
00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:51.257
Besides. my legs are like this.

116
00:09:51.841 --> 00:09:54.510
so I would've had trouble
with a higher floor.

117
00:10:04.186 --> 00:10:05.980
I love the look on your faces!

118
00:10:07.231 --> 00:10:08.524
<i>Do you think this is funny?</i>

119
00:10:10.192 --> 00:10:12.194
That little…

120
00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:13.112
What?

121
00:10:13.863 --> 00:10:15.156
No one's in the wrong here.

122
00:10:15.865 --> 00:10:17.658
Stop blaming each other.

123
00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:20.119
It's not like we picked
the higher floors on purpose.

124
00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:24.832
Today's cardio is done!

125
00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:30.254
Whether you get 10.000
or 340.000 won a minute. in the end.

126
00:10:30.755 --> 00:10:32.632
don't we all have the same goal?

127
00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:35.760
Keep the show going
for as long as possible

128
00:10:36.427 --> 00:10:38.012
and maximize our profit.

129
00:10:39.055 --> 00:10:40.181
Isn't that our goal?

130
00:10:40.264 --> 00:10:42.266
<i>This is fucked. but he's right.</i>

131
00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.976
If you're all done whining.

132
00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:46.562
shall we go eat?

133
00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:50.483
Right. Let's all go eat now.

134
00:10:50.566 --> 00:10:51.651
Come on. let's go.

135
00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:53.944
The food and water.

136
00:10:54.737 --> 00:10:56.113
How much will you send down?

137
00:11:02.119 --> 00:11:05.206
It's crappy enough to get paid less
for being on a lower floor.

138
00:11:05.289 --> 00:11:07.458
Do you want us to eat less too?

139
00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:09.669
Well. no.

140
00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:14.674
I thought of a way for us
to share the food equally.

141
00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.927
May I explain?

142
00:11:22.431 --> 00:11:25.142
<i>Each person takes one meal kit.</i>

143
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:30.147
<i>From the 8th floor to the 1st floor.</i>
<i>one per person. which is fair.</i>

144
00:11:32.233 --> 00:11:33.609
They look so good!

145
00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:35.820
<i>This show puts us in an extreme situation.</i>

146
00:11:36.612 --> 00:11:39.490
<i>Working as a community</i>
<i>is more vital than ever.</i>

147
00:11:41.242 --> 00:11:44.328
<i>We need to unite as one</i>
<i>and trust each other.</i>

148
00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:50.209
<i>That means there will be four left</i>
<i>after 1st Floor takes his.</i>

149
00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.169
What?

150
00:11:52.253 --> 00:11:54.422
Why are we giving him four more?

151
00:11:54.505 --> 00:11:56.590
No. That's not what we're doing.

152
00:11:57.341 --> 00:12:00.594
Nobody will be left starving
if we each take one.

153
00:12:01.929 --> 00:12:03.431
But if anyone wants more.

154
00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.643
you can come down to the 1st floor
and share what's left.

155
00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.439
<i>A system where no one's at a loss.</i>
<i>Everyone has to give up a little.</i>

156
00:12:11.522 --> 00:12:15.276
<i>but everyone can share the leftovers.</i>
<i>so no one loses out.</i>

157
00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.696
<i>Naturally. this will build trust among us.</i>

158
00:12:18.779 --> 00:12:20.531
Have the seasoned ones.

159
00:12:20.614 --> 00:12:21.782
-These?
-Yes.

160
00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:22.700
Why?

161
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.119
'Cause it's hot.

162
00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.705
-Are you finished?
-Eat up.

163
00:12:28.748 --> 00:12:30.166
Yum. It's good.

164
00:12:37.506 --> 00:12:40.050
Do you have any idea
what's in store for us?

165
00:12:40.676 --> 00:12:41.510
Sorry?

166
00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:44.638
We don't know what to expect.
so it's scarier.

167
00:12:45.222 --> 00:12:48.100
<i>Earlier. you said</i>
<i>you didn't know what to expect.</i>

168
00:12:49.143 --> 00:12:50.269
so you were scared.

169
00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:56.692
Yes. I think I have a rough idea
of what they want.

170
00:12:58.903 --> 00:13:00.321
-What's that?
-Hey!

171
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:02.948
What are you doing?

172
00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:06.202
What the hell are you doing?

173
00:13:06.285 --> 00:13:08.704
We only have 15 minutes left!

174
00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:20.216
Which one looks better?

175
00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:22.927
She didn't buy them with time. did she?

176
00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:27.264
Hey. If you want to buy clothes.
you should do it in your damn room!

177
00:13:27.348 --> 00:13:28.724
Why fucking buy them out here?

178
00:13:29.308 --> 00:13:31.644
Because if I do.
I can't wear them out here.

179
00:13:32.895 --> 00:13:34.605
I want to wear them out here.

180
00:13:35.898 --> 00:13:37.858
Why the swimsuit? There's no water.

181
00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:39.944
-For tanning.
-You crazy bitch.

182
00:13:40.694 --> 00:13:42.071
Do you have a death wish?

183
00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:44.156
Talk it out. Don't intimidate her.

184
00:13:49.787 --> 00:13:51.121
Is it because of this?

185
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.628
We can always extend that thing. Time.

186
00:13:58.712 --> 00:13:59.922
How would we do that?

187
00:14:01.715 --> 00:14:03.217
None of you know? Really?

188
00:14:04.051 --> 00:14:05.010
How to extend it?

189
00:14:08.097 --> 00:14:09.974
It's the stairs!

190
00:14:11.809 --> 00:14:13.185
-The stairs?
-Yes.

191
00:14:13.686 --> 00:14:15.688
There's a ton of stairs here.

192
00:14:16.397 --> 00:14:18.524
The time extends whenever we step on them.

193
00:14:20.526 --> 00:14:22.528
-Do you have proof?
-Proof?

194
00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:24.864
Wait. What was it again?

195
00:14:24.947 --> 00:14:26.782
Stop messing around and tell us.

196
00:14:28.325 --> 00:14:30.870
I'll tell you if you apologize to me.

197
00:14:30.953 --> 00:14:32.079
What?

198
00:14:32.162 --> 00:14:36.542
I'll tell you if you apologize
for cursing at me before.

199
00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:39.503
I'm so freaking sorry.
I apologize instead.

200
00:14:39.587 --> 00:14:41.297
We have no time. Tell us already!

201
00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.673
I guess that's a no.

202
00:14:43.299 --> 00:14:44.383
You motherfucker!

203
00:14:45.509 --> 00:14:46.427
Use your words.

204
00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.554
-What's your problem?
-Just get it over with.

205
00:14:48.637 --> 00:14:50.055
Can't you see everyone?

206
00:14:56.353 --> 00:14:58.063
-No!
-I can't let it end like this.

207
00:14:58.147 --> 00:15:00.232
This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity!

208
00:15:06.864 --> 00:15:09.366
Who cares if she's wrong?
We have less than ten minutes!

209
00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.201
-Okay.
-Let's give it a go.

210
00:15:32.514 --> 00:15:34.892
For fuck's sake! Are you sure this is it?

211
00:15:39.563 --> 00:15:40.606
It's still going down!

212
00:15:41.315 --> 00:15:42.983
Less than 30 seconds left!

213
00:16:09.176 --> 00:16:10.803
It's over? Just like that?

214
00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:18.310
Back to 24 hours!

215
00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:25.734
I told you. didn't I?

216
00:16:27.152 --> 00:16:28.445
I told you it's the stairs.

217
00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:30.447
That's what we've been doing.

218
00:16:30.531 --> 00:16:34.493
To check out my room and everyone else's
and to get the meal kits?

219
00:16:34.576 --> 00:16:37.204
I saw how the time extended then!

220
00:16:39.581 --> 00:16:41.375
I'm pretty smart. aren't I?

221
00:16:42.793 --> 00:16:44.837
<i>Just like that.</i>
<i>we discovered a hidden rule.</i>

222
00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.463
<i>Climbing stairs extends the time.</i>

223
00:16:46.547 --> 00:16:48.674
FOOD AND ACCOMMODATION PROVIDED
SPEND TIME TO EARN MONEY

224
00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:50.718
IT'S NOT DANGEROUS
CLIMBING THE STAIRS EXTENDS TIME

225
00:16:50.801 --> 00:16:52.261
<i>I thought it was all over.</i>

226
00:16:52.344 --> 00:16:53.554
<i>That was close.</i>

227
00:16:56.265 --> 00:16:59.643
<i>Yes. I think I have a rough idea</i>
<i>of what they want.</i>

228
00:17:00.144 --> 00:17:02.563
Conflict. They want us
to fight each other.

229
00:17:03.397 --> 00:17:05.691
Crises from the outside

230
00:17:07.151 --> 00:17:09.069
will only make us cooperate and persevere.

231
00:17:09.153 --> 00:17:10.529
But internal conflicts…

232
00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:14.283
If we fall apart internally.

233
00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:16.618
it's irreparable.

234
00:17:17.453 --> 00:17:20.539
<i>Yes. we need to stay united</i>
<i>through cooperation and perseverance.</i>

235
00:17:21.206 --> 00:17:23.917
<i>Man. that 7th Floor is one smart guy.</i>

236
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:27.546
I'll use this as long as possible
to avoid buying it again.

237
00:17:28.338 --> 00:17:29.173
Three…

238
00:17:31.008 --> 00:17:33.135
Two sheets should be enough.

239
00:17:42.561 --> 00:17:43.854
<i>It wasn't enough.</i>

240
00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.737
<i>It pisses me off</i>
<i>the more I think about it.</i>

241
00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:55.616
<i>I make 40 million every day.</i>
<i>I shouldn't skimp on things like this.</i>

242
00:17:55.699 --> 00:17:58.243
<i>Don't chicken out. Just buy it!</i>
<i>Yeah. let's do it!</i>

243
00:17:58.327 --> 00:18:01.747
Excuse me. I'm gonna go big here.
Get me a portable toilet.

244
00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.873
A simple one.

245
00:18:07.419 --> 00:18:08.462
Yes.

246
00:18:08.545 --> 00:18:09.463
Bring it.

247
00:18:17.054 --> 00:18:18.764
I can't get a refund. can I?

248
00:18:31.443 --> 00:18:32.569
That crazy bitch.

249
00:18:33.821 --> 00:18:37.324
I can't believe she bought clothes.
It pisses me off.

250
00:18:38.367 --> 00:18:40.410
Damn it. She's so annoying.

251
00:18:43.288 --> 00:18:44.748
We did great.

252
00:18:44.832 --> 00:18:48.001
This is all for us later.

253
00:18:48.085 --> 00:18:49.753
Look how much money we made.

254
00:19:10.858 --> 00:19:12.901
Okay. shall we get started?

255
00:19:13.735 --> 00:19:16.446
STAIR CLIMBING

256
00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.536
+210.000 WON
+20.000 WON

257
00:19:22.619 --> 00:19:24.204
+30.000 WON
+50.000 WON

258
00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:25.998
+340.000 WON
+80.000 WON

259
00:19:26.081 --> 00:19:27.791
+130.000 WON
+10.000 WON

260
00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:30.252
<i>After learning</i>
<i>that stair climbing extended our time.</i>

261
00:19:30.335 --> 00:19:31.420
<i>we climbed up and down</i>

262
00:19:31.503 --> 00:19:35.340
<i>until our hearts were about to burst</i>
<i>and our legs were shaking.</i>

263
00:19:36.258 --> 00:19:38.719
<i>The more time we gained.</i>
<i>the hungrier people got.</i>

264
00:19:38.802 --> 00:19:40.304
<i>so the 1st floor became popular.</i>

265
00:19:50.981 --> 00:19:52.691
<i>We were worn out every night.</i>

266
00:19:53.525 --> 00:19:54.943
<i>but we couldn't complain.</i>

267
00:20:22.387 --> 00:20:24.389
I don't even feel like I've eaten.

268
00:20:25.641 --> 00:20:27.226
Eating once a day

269
00:20:27.309 --> 00:20:30.604
and nibbling on leftover food like this
is barely enough.

270
00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:34.274
We go up and down those stairs
over and over every day.

271
00:20:34.358 --> 00:20:35.359
It's all too harsh.

272
00:20:35.859 --> 00:20:38.111
Even if the prices
were 1.000 times higher.

273
00:20:38.612 --> 00:20:40.030
I'd like to buy some food.

274
00:20:42.991 --> 00:20:46.411
-Like those hot dogs downstairs.
-I want burgers.

275
00:20:46.495 --> 00:20:47.746
Fried chicken for me.

276
00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.417
Let's split up.

277
00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:56.213
We should divide our work.

278
00:20:58.882 --> 00:21:02.636
So you want us to split into two teams
and climb the stairs every other day?

279
00:21:02.719 --> 00:21:05.055
Yes. We can work one day.
then rest the next.

280
00:21:05.138 --> 00:21:08.141
We'll give the leftover food
to the team that worked.

281
00:21:08.225 --> 00:21:10.102
The working team can get two meals a day.

282
00:21:10.185 --> 00:21:12.271
A single meal should be enough
on days off.

283
00:21:12.354 --> 00:21:14.314
Yes. I agree with this.

284
00:21:15.983 --> 00:21:19.528
One meal is enough when we're not working.
It's better to rest. isn't it?

285
00:21:20.028 --> 00:21:21.113
I agree.

286
00:21:22.114 --> 00:21:22.948
Same here.

287
00:21:23.532 --> 00:21:24.700
Let's try it.

288
00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.495
We'll see how much time we get.

289
00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.043
How about we split up like this?

290
00:21:39.339 --> 00:21:40.549
I'm switching teams.

291
00:21:41.383 --> 00:21:42.342
We don't get along.

292
00:21:44.886 --> 00:21:45.762
Me?

293
00:21:49.182 --> 00:21:52.311
Is anyone willing
to switch teams with 2nd Floor?

294
00:21:52.394 --> 00:21:55.188
<i>The whiny chick. The thug.</i>

295
00:21:55.856 --> 00:21:56.732
<i>The wacko.</i>

296
00:21:56.815 --> 00:21:57.733
THUG. WHINY CHICK

297
00:21:57.816 --> 00:22:00.235
<i>Who'd want to join that team?</i>
<i>The members speak for themselves.</i>

298
00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:03.655
Excuse me. I don't mind which team I'm on.

299
00:22:14.416 --> 00:22:15.876
This is nice.

300
00:22:15.959 --> 00:22:19.129
Two men on each team is perfect. isn't it?

301
00:22:19.212 --> 00:22:20.339
Yes. this is great.

302
00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:24.426
<i>It was an excellent idea</i>
<i>to split into two teams.</i>

303
00:22:25.135 --> 00:22:27.846
<i>Despite the hard work.</i>
<i>the prospect of resting the next day</i>

304
00:22:27.929 --> 00:22:30.140
<i>is enough motivation.</i>

305
00:22:32.768 --> 00:22:34.436
<i>And the best part is</i>

306
00:22:34.519 --> 00:22:37.689
<i>you can eat to your heart's content</i>
<i>on the days you work.</i>

307
00:22:38.315 --> 00:22:41.026
<i>"Those who do not work shall not eat."</i>

308
00:22:48.492 --> 00:22:50.744
-Are you okay?
-I almost hurt my back!

309
00:22:50.827 --> 00:22:52.245
I'm sorry. 4th Floor.

310
00:22:52.329 --> 00:22:53.955
-Whatever.
-I'm really sorry.

311
00:22:54.498 --> 00:22:56.416
I'm so sorry. Really.

312
00:23:00.962 --> 00:23:01.797
Are you okay?

313
00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:08.678
Yeah. I'm okay.

314
00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:21.942
Wipe that smile off your face
and get to work.

315
00:23:22.818 --> 00:23:25.445
We're not gaining any time because of you.

316
00:23:26.613 --> 00:23:27.656
What are you doing?

317
00:24:00.897 --> 00:24:01.773
I'll fill in.

318
00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:04.484
Sorry?

319
00:24:04.568 --> 00:24:06.445
Get some rest. I'll fill in for you.

320
00:24:09.239 --> 00:24:10.157
Any objections?

321
00:24:15.537 --> 00:24:17.122
-No. I can--
-Forget it.

322
00:24:18.415 --> 00:24:20.208
I feel stiff when I don't exercise.

323
00:24:20.292 --> 00:24:21.126
I can…

324
00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:24.754
How admirable.

325
00:24:28.884 --> 00:24:30.886
THE NEXT DAY

326
00:24:54.159 --> 00:24:56.411
You must be tired
from working two days in a row.

327
00:24:56.995 --> 00:24:57.871
It's fine.

328
00:25:03.376 --> 00:25:05.587
THE DAY AFTER

329
00:25:24.898 --> 00:25:25.774
<i>Should I help</i>

330
00:25:26.566 --> 00:25:27.400
<i>or not?</i>

331
00:25:28.902 --> 00:25:31.154
<i>Should I help or not?</i>

332
00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:35.367
<i>Help? Or not? Should I help or not?</i>

333
00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:38.036
<i>Should I help or not? Help or not? Wait…</i>

334
00:25:38.119 --> 00:25:39.955
Oh! Excuse me! Mr. 1st Floor.

335
00:25:50.215 --> 00:25:53.260
Please go rest. 1st Floor. I'll do it.

336
00:25:53.343 --> 00:25:54.469
Sorry. what?

337
00:25:54.553 --> 00:25:55.679
Goodness. no.

338
00:25:55.762 --> 00:25:57.430
-No. let me.
-I have to do it today.

339
00:25:57.514 --> 00:26:01.226
Really. Look. I ate too much yesterday.

340
00:26:01.309 --> 00:26:03.186
I'm having trouble digesting.

341
00:26:03.687 --> 00:26:07.023
Yeah. so please go rest and recover.

342
00:26:07.107 --> 00:26:07.983
Goodness.

343
00:26:08.733 --> 00:26:09.943
I'm so sorry.

344
00:26:10.026 --> 00:26:10.902
It's really fine.

345
00:26:11.861 --> 00:26:13.363
Sorry. let me through.

346
00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:16.575
Excuse me. Coming through.

347
00:26:17.993 --> 00:26:20.495
God. we're all tired too.

348
00:26:21.288 --> 00:26:23.540
We're all running
like our lives depend on it.

349
00:26:37.762 --> 00:26:39.306
-Please have a seat.
-Sit here.

350
00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:42.517
<i>Shouldering extra work for a teammate.</i>

351
00:26:43.018 --> 00:26:44.019
<i>How awesome am I?</i>

352
00:26:45.186 --> 00:26:46.021
I got this!

353
00:26:52.569 --> 00:26:55.614
3rd Floor. You can't be here like this.

354
00:26:56.448 --> 00:26:59.075
-Let's go.
-Wait. give me five more seconds.

355
00:27:01.661 --> 00:27:03.038
Come on. Let's get up.

356
00:27:03.121 --> 00:27:03.955
It's not…

357
00:27:04.039 --> 00:27:04.873
Try to get up.

358
00:27:05.373 --> 00:27:06.708
Gently. please. Yeah.

359
00:27:09.794 --> 00:27:11.129
Please have a bite to eat.

360
00:27:11.212 --> 00:27:12.255
Enjoy your meal.

361
00:27:12.339 --> 00:27:13.173
Thank you.

362
00:27:14.174 --> 00:27:15.008
This way.

363
00:27:15.508 --> 00:27:16.718
You're going to eat?

364
00:27:17.802 --> 00:27:18.637
Sorry?

365
00:27:19.137 --> 00:27:20.555
Are you actually gonna eat?

366
00:27:23.975 --> 00:27:25.727
Come on. 4th Floor.

367
00:27:26.978 --> 00:27:29.939
I mean. honestly speaking.

368
00:27:30.023 --> 00:27:32.901
shouldn't 3rd Floor be eating instead?

369
00:27:34.361 --> 00:27:37.989
Do you really need both meals
when you haven't even worked?

370
00:27:41.284 --> 00:27:42.786
Think you're clever. don't you?

371
00:27:44.162 --> 00:27:46.581
You have one extra
since 8th Floor doesn't eat anyway.

372
00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:49.334
Why are you tripping?

373
00:27:52.629 --> 00:27:55.090
I'm not saying you shouldn't eat.

374
00:27:55.715 --> 00:27:58.551
You know? I was just saying it's not fair.

375
00:28:01.554 --> 00:28:02.389
You should eat--

376
00:28:14.526 --> 00:28:16.611
3rd Floor. please go on in.

377
00:28:16.695 --> 00:28:18.279
You worked instead of me today.

378
00:28:19.406 --> 00:28:21.366
-Sure.
-Don't be ridiculous.

379
00:28:22.659 --> 00:28:25.203
You think we worked instead of you
for the fucking food?

380
00:28:25.829 --> 00:28:28.248
You think he could eat this
with a clear conscience?

381
00:28:28.331 --> 00:28:29.165
Am I wrong?

382
00:28:31.668 --> 00:28:32.669
No. you're right.

383
00:28:34.796 --> 00:28:36.548
Don't mind them. Just go eat.

384
00:28:37.632 --> 00:28:40.885
They're just bitching
because they're fed up and tired.

385
00:28:43.430 --> 00:28:44.472
Yes. she's right.

386
00:28:45.598 --> 00:28:48.727
You should go and eat. 1st Floor.
It's just how it is.

387
00:28:48.810 --> 00:28:51.020
No need to mind me. Yeah.

388
00:28:51.771 --> 00:28:53.189
No. Please.

389
00:28:57.777 --> 00:28:59.154
Go on. You should go and--

390
00:28:59.237 --> 00:29:02.824
Come on. Just go in and eat.

391
00:29:02.907 --> 00:29:04.617
-Thank you. 3rd Floor.
-Sure.

392
00:29:04.701 --> 00:29:06.369
-No. still. he--
-Come on.

393
00:29:06.453 --> 00:29:08.872
Just go eat. He said he was fine with it.

394
00:29:10.832 --> 00:29:11.875
Are you okay?

395
00:29:13.293 --> 00:29:14.586
Of course.

396
00:29:14.669 --> 00:29:16.921
Because of this asshole.

397
00:29:17.005 --> 00:29:19.299
I ended up coming
to this godforsaken place…

398
00:29:19.382 --> 00:29:20.216
IN YOU. I TRUST

399
00:29:20.300 --> 00:29:23.428
…and climbing a lifetime's worth
of stairs. you son of a bitch.

400
00:29:23.511 --> 00:29:24.846
WEASEL

401
00:29:24.929 --> 00:29:26.514
It's all your fault.

402
00:29:30.727 --> 00:29:31.853
My legs.

403
00:29:35.648 --> 00:29:36.524
Food is here.

404
00:29:43.907 --> 00:29:45.116
What's all this?

405
00:29:47.452 --> 00:29:49.204
Seriously. what the hell?

406
00:29:49.287 --> 00:29:50.872
-3rd Floor.
-Yes?

407
00:29:56.878 --> 00:29:57.879
Something fell. right?

408
00:29:58.379 --> 00:30:01.966
I thought it was food.
but they sent down poop bags!

409
00:30:02.050 --> 00:30:04.636
-For God's sake.
-1st Floor said to send them down.

410
00:30:05.136 --> 00:30:07.180
I've given it some thought.

411
00:30:08.431 --> 00:30:10.433
Since I'm not great at climbing stairs

412
00:30:10.934 --> 00:30:12.644
and people keep filling in for me.

413
00:30:13.144 --> 00:30:16.564
I thought of what I could do to help.

414
00:30:16.648 --> 00:30:18.525
And. well…

415
00:30:18.608 --> 00:30:20.193
<i>1st Floor said he was torn up</i>

416
00:30:20.276 --> 00:30:22.862
<i>about how he was impeding us</i>
<i>due to his condition.</i>

417
00:30:22.946 --> 00:30:26.324
I thought we'd be even
if you all sent down…

418
00:30:28.368 --> 00:30:29.744
your waste bags to me.

419
00:30:31.329 --> 00:30:32.288
Really?

420
00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:51.516
<i>While pondering what he could do</i>
<i>for the team instead of physical labor.</i>

421
00:30:51.599 --> 00:30:53.893
<i>he said the delivery chute caught his eye.</i>

422
00:30:55.562 --> 00:31:01.651
<i>It occurred to him that we could send</i>
<i>things other than meal kits through it.</i>

423
00:31:04.404 --> 00:31:09.117
<i>1st Floor's proposal and our acceptance</i>
<i>established a sanitary worker among us.</i>

424
00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:13.288
<i>When everyone fulfills their roles.</i>

425
00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:16.207
<i>society reaches equilibrium</i>
<i>and functions smoothly.</i>

426
00:31:17.750 --> 00:31:19.669
<i>And 1st Floor had found it.</i>

427
00:31:21.254 --> 00:31:23.756
<i>A newfound self-value worth bartering.</i>

428
00:31:39.105 --> 00:31:41.524
<i>Those less prone to hunger</i>
<i>share their food.</i>

429
00:31:44.360 --> 00:31:45.278
Get some rest.

430
00:31:47.238 --> 00:31:48.281
I'll take it from here.

431
00:31:48.364 --> 00:31:50.575
<i>Those with fitter bodies</i>
<i>share their manpower.</i>

432
00:31:52.535 --> 00:31:55.914
<i>Those who can't share those things</i>
<i>offer their space for communal use.</i>

433
00:31:56.539 --> 00:31:59.125
<i>All in all. it's a pretty fair deal.</i>

434
00:32:02.128 --> 00:32:03.087
I'll see you later.

435
00:32:04.047 --> 00:32:06.424
Hello. 1st Floor.

436
00:32:08.051 --> 00:32:10.386
This will make it
more comfortable for you.

437
00:32:10.887 --> 00:32:13.806
There's no need. We're fine.
Please do it later.

438
00:32:24.192 --> 00:32:26.027
Are you done eating. 3rd Floor?

439
00:32:26.527 --> 00:32:29.489
Not yet. I think I ate too fast.
I don't feel good.

440
00:32:29.572 --> 00:32:30.406
I see.

441
00:32:36.788 --> 00:32:37.997
What are you looking at?

442
00:32:38.081 --> 00:32:40.083
The time…

443
00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:44.420
It has been extending irregularly lately.

444
00:32:45.964 --> 00:32:49.592
It shot up before midnight yesterday.
but now it has stopped increasing.

445
00:32:50.885 --> 00:32:53.388
Do you think
it's because we're not climbing enough?

446
00:32:53.471 --> 00:32:56.140
I'm not sure. Everyone's doing their job.

447
00:33:02.647 --> 00:33:06.442
Did you see that?
We just got ten more minutes.

448
00:33:07.026 --> 00:33:10.446
But everyone's taking a break
after the meal.

449
00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:11.614
Did someone go up?

450
00:33:26.754 --> 00:33:29.716
Fuck. What's wrong with that thing?

451
00:33:32.051 --> 00:33:35.263
I told you.
They're getting stingier with time.

452
00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:37.515
It's barely going up.

453
00:33:38.891 --> 00:33:41.602
Do they want us
to ramp up the workload or what?

454
00:33:42.478 --> 00:33:43.938
We're not Olympic athletes.

455
00:33:46.607 --> 00:33:47.608
I'm over this.

456
00:33:49.027 --> 00:33:50.820
-I'm sorry?
-What?

457
00:33:50.903 --> 00:33:52.488
I'm not doing this anymore.

458
00:33:53.531 --> 00:33:56.075
But we can't just stop working.

459
00:33:56.159 --> 00:33:57.326
What are you doing?

460
00:33:57.410 --> 00:33:59.078
It's not fun anymore.

461
00:33:59.620 --> 00:34:00.997
Good luck. you three.

462
00:34:01.080 --> 00:34:02.498
Just shut up and do it!

463
00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:04.876
Why should I?

464
00:34:08.421 --> 00:34:11.591
Hey. Shouldn't you be working harder
than the rest of us?

465
00:34:12.675 --> 00:34:15.261
You make way more than we do.

466
00:34:15.344 --> 00:34:18.139
Shouldn't you put in
a bit more effort than us?

467
00:34:22.101 --> 00:34:24.979
Shouldn't you
and the people on the lower floors

468
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:27.523
work harder instead?

469
00:34:27.607 --> 00:34:28.941
What?

470
00:34:29.025 --> 00:34:30.068
Think about it.

471
00:34:30.610 --> 00:34:32.862
You don't want to use your money.

472
00:34:32.945 --> 00:34:36.532
so you've used our shared time
to buy toilet paper. wet wipes.

473
00:34:36.616 --> 00:34:37.617
and other necessities.

474
00:34:37.700 --> 00:34:40.369
Technically.
if we're using time to buy items.

475
00:34:40.453 --> 00:34:44.415
aren't those on the top floors
paying far more than you guys?

476
00:34:44.499 --> 00:34:45.750
<i>That wacko</i>…

477
00:34:45.833 --> 00:34:47.835
After all. time is money here.

478
00:34:47.919 --> 00:34:49.587
<i>…isn't wrong.</i>

479
00:34:50.463 --> 00:34:53.341
<i>An hour is only worth</i>
<i>1.2 million won to 2nd Floor.</i>

480
00:34:53.424 --> 00:34:56.094
<i>but worth a whopping 20.4 million won</i>
<i>to 8th Floor.</i>

481
00:34:57.887 --> 00:34:59.847
<i>Since we're using the time we share.</i>

482
00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:02.767
<i>the higher floors</i>
<i>are technically spending more money.</i>

483
00:35:03.392 --> 00:35:06.187
<i>I didn't take her as a thinker.</i>
<i>She's surprisingly sharp.</i>

484
00:35:06.896 --> 00:35:10.316
Let's keep climbing the stairs
instead of wasting time arguing.

485
00:35:10.983 --> 00:35:12.693
The show's going to end at this rate!

486
00:35:12.777 --> 00:35:14.946
Hey. let's climb with them.

487
00:35:15.530 --> 00:35:16.697
We should help out.

488
00:35:16.781 --> 00:35:19.617
Are you sure
climbing stairs gives us more time?

489
00:35:19.700 --> 00:35:20.535
What?

490
00:35:21.035 --> 00:35:22.036
It's strange.

491
00:35:22.662 --> 00:35:25.414
We've been climbing the stairs
at the same rate.

492
00:35:32.046 --> 00:35:33.089
That crazy bitch.

493
00:35:53.860 --> 00:35:56.654
We've actually lost time
instead of earning it.

494
00:35:57.238 --> 00:36:00.867
What if it doesn't go up anymore?

495
00:36:01.909 --> 00:36:02.743
You're right.

496
00:36:03.703 --> 00:36:05.955
We've been at this for over six hours.

497
00:36:07.248 --> 00:36:08.499
We haven't earned a minute.

498
00:36:08.583 --> 00:36:10.918
It'll be midnight soon.
so we must go to our rooms.

499
00:36:11.419 --> 00:36:12.962
We can't do more today.

500
00:36:14.172 --> 00:36:15.923
What? It just went up.

501
00:36:18.092 --> 00:36:19.969
Hey. it just went up!

502
00:36:20.052 --> 00:36:21.220
-Twenty minutes?
-Finally!

503
00:36:21.304 --> 00:36:22.722
Wasn't that 20 minutes?

504
00:36:22.805 --> 00:36:24.348
It must be lagging.

505
00:36:24.432 --> 00:36:25.933
I guess it's working again now.

506
00:36:26.017 --> 00:36:27.560
Hey. I knew it.

507
00:36:27.643 --> 00:36:29.937
We were worried for no reason. I knew it.

508
00:36:30.021 --> 00:36:31.647
-What a relief.
-Yeah.

509
00:36:31.731 --> 00:36:33.482
I'm so glad.

510
00:36:34.442 --> 00:36:37.028
I guess it'll go up.
even if it takes time.

511
00:36:37.612 --> 00:36:38.654
It's midnight.

512
00:36:40.072 --> 00:36:40.907
Let's all go in.

513
00:36:41.782 --> 00:36:42.783
Great job today.

514
00:36:49.457 --> 00:36:51.334
Let's go inside. Good work.

515
00:37:29.789 --> 00:37:33.084
Everyone. come outside! Get out here!

516
00:37:34.460 --> 00:37:37.421
I don't think we've been rewarded
our time. Hurry up. and come out!

517
00:37:37.505 --> 00:37:38.714
Everyone. start running.

518
00:37:38.798 --> 00:37:40.132
Everyone!

519
00:37:40.216 --> 00:37:42.051
Let's run. everybody.

520
00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:45.388
But we didn't even get our time
for yesterday's work.

521
00:37:45.471 --> 00:37:47.181
What if it's of no use again?

522
00:37:47.265 --> 00:37:49.392
Still. it's the only option we have.

523
00:37:49.475 --> 00:37:51.310
Start climbing the stairs. everyone!

524
00:37:55.356 --> 00:37:57.024
This is fucking bullshit.

525
00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:13.291
-She fell on her back!
-4th Floor!

526
00:38:13.374 --> 00:38:14.542
-What?
-She just--

527
00:38:14.625 --> 00:38:15.543
Hold on.

528
00:38:15.626 --> 00:38:17.378
-It's an epileptic seizure.
-What?

529
00:38:17.461 --> 00:38:20.006
It's epilepsy! Don't touch her!

530
00:38:20.798 --> 00:38:22.883
-Oh. epilepsy.
-Wait. we need to--

531
00:38:22.967 --> 00:38:24.427
Do you have medical training?

532
00:38:25.261 --> 00:38:28.055
-Yes. I was a nurse.
-Is there medicine for this?

533
00:38:28.139 --> 00:38:29.557
She needs Phenytoin.

534
00:38:37.773 --> 00:38:38.816
Stay where you are.

535
00:38:38.899 --> 00:38:40.192
What are you saying?

536
00:38:40.276 --> 00:38:42.028
Don't do anything. She won't die.

537
00:38:42.862 --> 00:38:43.696
What?

538
00:38:44.196 --> 00:38:45.781
Epilepsy doesn't kill.

539
00:38:45.865 --> 00:38:48.242
Leaving her like this for so long
may damage her brain.

540
00:38:48.326 --> 00:38:49.869
The medicine won't be cheap.

541
00:38:49.952 --> 00:38:53.456
If we use up the little time we have.
the game is over!

542
00:38:53.539 --> 00:38:55.333
You're not even human.

543
00:38:57.710 --> 00:38:59.170
Don't get in my fucking way.

544
00:39:53.307 --> 00:39:56.102
We need medicine for epilepsy! Phenytoin!

545
00:40:11.742 --> 00:40:12.993
This is too funny.

546
00:40:15.538 --> 00:40:17.373
Don't you see what I see?

547
00:40:17.873 --> 00:40:19.625
Don't you all see that?

548
00:40:23.129 --> 00:40:25.005
Forty hours?

549
00:40:28.092 --> 00:40:30.719
This is so much fun.

550
00:40:30.803 --> 00:40:32.096
It wasn't the stairs

551
00:40:33.889 --> 00:40:35.182
that gave us more time.

552
00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:36.350
Then what was it?

553
00:40:48.404 --> 00:40:49.405
What. then?

554
00:40:50.364 --> 00:40:51.699
What gives us more time?

555
00:40:52.741 --> 00:40:53.617
It must be…

556
00:40:56.871 --> 00:40:58.164
entertaining to watch.

557
00:41:39.497 --> 00:41:45.294
PHENYTOIN

558
00:41:46.305 --> 00:42:46.781
